# ECB Architecture Rules

## Layer Responsibilities
- Boundary: external input/output (CLI, API, UI).
- Control: business use cases and orchestration.
- Entity: domain models and business rules only.

## Dependency Direction
- boundary -> control
- control -> entity
- entity -> no dependency on boundary or control

## Layer Constraints
- Boundary must not call Entity directly; route through Control.
- Control must not depend on Boundary implementation details.
- Entity must remain pure domain logic with no external I/O.

## Recommended Structure
- `src/boundary/cli`, `src/boundary/api`
- `src/control/use_cases`, `src/control/services`
- `src/entity/models`, `src/entity/rules`
- `tests/boundary`, `tests/control`, `tests/entity`, `tests/integration`
